L4-E2: THE ENERGY ARCHITECTURE REPLAY UNDER REQ-016'S 100 W WINDOW (l4e_replay.py, layer 4, MESHSAT-1357).
PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing built, bought, powered or measured. MODELED on a1elec's energy_two_pack.py through l3plane's
energy_basis.py set-up (both pinned, imported unchanged). The corrected power path is HYPOTHETICAL; every WE figure is
CONDITIONAL on the three undocumented efficiencies (C-8). The author's analysis, AI arithmetic; not a qualified review and
not the independent check.

0. REPRODUCTION (before any result)
   0a l3batt's runtime.py re-run in a child process reproduces runtime.out byte for byte (sha256 87d9c1ee59059763): yes
   0b this harness reproduces runtime.out section 1's D06 and A35 rows, the twenty cells of section 2 (400 Wp, 200 W) and
      section 3's 12 least-lid lines (48 and 72 h; NOM, WE, NOM90; TYP and WAB): yes
   0c this harness reproduces three_cases.out's AS DRAWN rows at WE inputs, the both-kept lid, 72 h: TYP 589.3, WAB 616.7 Wh
      unserved: yes
   0d the single-pack use (the lid off) reproduces energy_budget.out 5b, PS-IDLE-SPEC, September, a 100 Wp panel in the
      100 W window on the record's own chain: 06 UTC usable 107.9 Wh, first stop h 8, 23 h run, 1870.8 Wh unserved; 18 UTC first
      stop h 2, 23 h run, 1781.9 Wh unserved: yes (so 'full service' below counts hours as the record's 'h run' does)

1. THE ONE ASSUMPTION SET (both architectures; only the stage window differs from runtime.out section 2)
   load       PS-IDLE-SPEC 42.8 W at the pack terminals over its 39 loads (REQ-072's objective_profile); HF available, not
              receiving; the tablet not charged, the USB-C outlet off; A2 adds the lid path's standby drain 0.025 W (WE)
   store      full at the start, aged to 80 % (REQ-014), each pack to its 3.00 V line with the 5 % reserve; the base at
              +20 C, A2's lid at 13.23 C (SC-37's air minimum); battery-only both at +20 C, then both at -10 C
   sun        SC-37's mean September day at Leiden, one plane 40/0, repeated; TYP the case, WAB a sensitivity (build ratio
              0.9903 / 0.9103 on PVGIS's 0.9417); starts 06 and 18 UTC; the availability series is the checked 400 Wp 2S2P trace
   window     the stage's input clipped at REQ-016's 100 W (energy_inputs.yaml: 'REQ-016 (SC-36): at most 100 W into board E's LT8705A stage;')
