5. THE ENERGY ACCOUNT, TYP, 72 h, the 100 W window (Wh over the run; per start; kit and per pack)
   array = the 400 Wp trace at the array; clip = above the window; stage in = into the stage; bus = at VBUS20 before the
   entry's cap (stage and front end losses taken); not taken = refused by the entry's cap or its collapse; U3 = U3's loss;
   node = at the system node; to load = the node's sun used by the load in the hour; accepted = taken into charge at the
   node; spill = offered to charge but refused (packs full or tapering, or the charge ceiling); stored = into the cells;
   chg loss = accepted less stored (U3B, the lid loop, the 0.95 charge efficiency); drawn = out of the cells; lid path =
   the lid's discharge path loss; cut = the first hour each pack stands at its line (the kit's stop puts both there);
   closure = start + stored - drawn - end
