7. WHAT THE 100 W RESULT REPRESENTS: the series is the 400 Wp 2S2P trace (a1solar's build, fixed point 34.29 V, ratio 0.9903 TYP)
   the stimulus: 1497.5 Wh a day at the array (peak 194.3 W); 1497.5 Wh into the stage at 200 W; 982.6 Wh at 100 W, clipped in 8 hours
   at the node on WE: 827.1 Wh a day through the 100 W window; the window's ceiling with a 20 kWp array (energy_budget.out 4's
   method, on WE's chain) 1016.8. PS-IDLE-SPEC asks 1027.2 Wh a day at the pack terminals (1027.8 with A2's drain): under WE no
   array carries the day's demand through this window, so each day ends shorter than it began and the store must hold the
   first night plus each later day's deficit (at the node, before charge losses, 200.1 Wh a day with the stimulus)
   the array needed to reach 100 W in an hour at the trace's ratio: 06 UTC 1865 Wp, 07 UTC 560 Wp, 08 UTC 326 Wp, 09 UTC 243 Wp, 10 UTC 213 Wp, 11 UTC 208 Wp, 12 UTC 206 Wp, 13 UTC 222 Wp, 14 UTC 263 Wp, 15 UTC 331 Wp, 16 UTC 568 Wp
   REQ-016 admits a panel of at most 25 V open circuit at its coldest, held at 17.6 V, at most 100 W into the stage
   (acceptance: a bench supply on a 100 W panel's curve, MPP 17.6 V, Voc 25 V). The trace is 2S2P at 34.29 V: 51.28 V cold
   (a1solar ARRAY.md 1), outside it. The held panel is outside it even alone (25.64 V at -20 C cells); a1solar ARRAY.md 5
   reads the SunPower (24.05 V) and PowerFilm's 15 V model (24.86 V) as admitted at -20 C, none at -40 C; neither has an
   availability trace in the tree. The records read an array above about 150 Wp of the 12 V class as re-rating the
   entry's 10 A (energy_budget.out 4), which REQ-016's acceptance names. So the 100 W result is a CONDITIONAL SCREENING
   STIMULUS: it stands for a compliant source only if one delivers, in every hour, at least min(the 400 Wp trace, 100 W).
   Sensitivity on the held panel's fit held at 17.6 V (a1solar's ratio method, INFERRED; the panel itself is not compliant):
